; Default metric definitions
;
; Metrics are used to declare what types of measurements will be tracked in the
; plain-text-health data store.
;
; Definition syntax:
; metric <name> <unit> [additive] [metadata]
;
; [additive] is an optional flag that indicates measures should be summed if
; multiple are defined over the same period. (ex. for sleep hours, naps should
; add to the total sum of sleep for the day)
;
; [metadata] is an optional set of key:value properties. They may be added on
; indented newlines for formatting cleanliness.
;
; Aliases provide a convenient way to declare multiple measurements in a single
; entry. For example, if blood pressure is defined as two measures, bp_sys and
; bp_dia, you can define an alias to record both values in one line:
;
; metric bp = bp_sys / bp_dia
;
; The syntax for declaring an alias is:
;
; metric <name> = <metric_a> / <metric_b> [/ <metric_c> ...]
;

metric weight   lb               range: 50..500
metric bodyfat  %                 range: 3..60
metric steps    steps   additive  range: 0..100000
metric sleep    hr      additive  range: 0..24
metric bp_sys   mmHg              range: 60..250
metric bp_dia   mmHg              range: 30..150
metric bp = bp_sys / bp_dia